@startuml
title Tab A does not know tab B — the browser forwards the event
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #93C5FD
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
participant "Tab A\nOwn session store" as A
database "Browser\nlocalStorage + event delivery" as Browser
participant "Tab B\nOwn session store" as B
B -> B : Provider calls session.subscribeToChanges()\nRegister window storage listener
... User signs out in A ...
A -> A : Controller clears local session\nController announces SignedOut
A -> Browser : setItem(session event,\n{event: signed-out, nonce: ...})
Browser -> B : storage event
B -> B : Check key, parse message\nValidate event name
B -> B : externalSessionChanged(true)\nClear local session; block restoration
note over A,B
The sender gets no storage event from its own write.
The message contains no credentials.
Only other listening documents sharing this storage area participate.
end note
note over Browser,B
Same origin = same scheme, host and port.
No cross-device or cross-profile delivery.
No replay of missed events; storage writes can fail.
end note
@enduml
